---Specifies options for controlling advanced machine features. Options that would traditionally be configured in a BIOS belong here. Features that require operating system support may have corresponding entries in the GuestOsFeatures of an Image (e.g., whether or not the OS in the Image supports nested virtualization being enabled or disabled).
---@class azure.gcpconnector.AdvancedMachineFeatures
---@field enableNestedVirtualization? boolean Whether to enable nested virtualization or not (default is false).
---@field enableUefiNetworking? boolean Whether to enable UEFI networking for instance creation.
---@field threadsPerCore? number The number of threads per physical core. To disable simultaneous multithreading (SMT) set this to 1. If unset, the maximum number of threads supported per core by the underlying processor is assumed.
---@field visibleCoreCount? number The number of physical cores to expose to an instance. Multiply by the number of threads per core to compute the total number of virtual CPUs to expose to the instance. If unset, the number of cores is inferred from the instance's nominal CPU count and the underlying platform's SMT width.

---Specifies options for controlling advanced machine features
---@class azure.gcpconnector.AdvancedMachineFeatures_2
---@field threadsPerCore? string The number of threads per physical core
---@field enableNestedVirtualization? boolean Whether or not to enable nested virtualization

---An alias IP range attached to an instance's network interface.
---@class azure.gcpconnector.AliasIpRange
---@field ipCidrRange? string The IP alias ranges to allocate for this interface. This IP CIDR range must belong to the specified subnetwork and cannot contain IP addresses reserved by system or used by other network interfaces. This range may be a single IP address (such as 10.2.3.4), a netmask (such as /24) or a CIDR-formatted string (such as 10.1.2.0/24).
---@field subnetworkRangeName? string The name of a subnetwork secondary IP range from which to allocate an IP alias range. If not specified, the primary range of the subnetwork is used.

