---Filters events based on exact matches on the CloudEvents attributes.
---@class azure.gcpconnector.EventFilter
---@field attribute? string Required. The name of a CloudEvents attribute.
---@field operator? string Optional. The operator used for matching the events with the value of the filter. If not specified, only events that have an exact key-value pair specified in the filter are matched. The only allowed value is `match-path-pattern`.
---@field value? string Required. The value for the attribute.

---Describes EventTrigger, used to request events to be sent from another service.
---@class azure.gcpconnector.EventTrigger
---@field channel? string Optional. The name of the channel associated with the trigger in `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/channels/{channel}` format. You must provide a channel to receive events from Eventarc SaaS partners.
---@field eventFilters? azure.gcpconnector.EventTriggerEventFiltersList Criteria used to filter events.
---@field eventType? string Required. The type of event to observe. For example: `google.cloud.audit.log.v1.written` or `google.cloud.pubsub.topic.v1.messagePublished`.
---@field pubsubTopic? string Optional. The name of a Pub/Sub topic in the same project that will be used as the transport topic for the event delivery. Format: `projects/{project}/topics/{topic}`. This is only valid for events of type `google.cloud.pubsub.topic.v1.messagePublished`. The topic provided here will not be deleted at function deletion.
---@field retryPolicy? azure.gcpconnector.RetryPolicy|string Optional. If unset, then defaults to ignoring failures (i.e. not retrying them).
---@field service? string Optional. The hostname of the service that 1st Gen function should be observed. If no string is provided, the default service implementing the API will be used. For example, `storage.googleapis.com` is the default for all event types in the `google.storage` namespace. The field is only applicable to 1st Gen functions.
---@field serviceAccountEmail? string Optional. The email of the trigger's service account. The service account must have permission to invoke Cloud Run services, the permission is `run.routes.invoke`. If empty, defaults to the Compute Engine default service account: `{project_number}-compute@developer.gserviceaccount.com`.
---@field trigger? string Output only. The resource name of the Eventarc trigger. The format of this field is `projects/{project}/locations/{region}/triggers/{trigger}`.
---@field triggerRegion? string The region that the trigger will be in. The trigger will only receive events originating in this region. It can be the same region as the function, a different region or multi-region, or the global region. If not provided, defaults to the same region as the function.

---Criteria used to filter events.
---@alias azure.gcpconnector.EventTriggerEventFiltersList azure.gcpconnector.EventFilter[]

