---A bucket.
---@class azure.gcpconnector.GcpBucketProperties
---@field acl? azure.gcpconnector.GcpBucketPropertiesAclList Access controls on the bucket.
---@field autoclass? azure.gcpconnector.GcpBucketPropertiesAutoclass The bucket's Autoclass configuration.
---@field billing? azure.gcpconnector.GcpBucketPropertiesBilling The bucket's billing configuration.
---@field cors? azure.gcpconnector.GcpBucketPropertiesCorsList The bucket's Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) configuration.
---@field customPlacementConfig? azure.gcpconnector.GcpBucketPropertiesCustomPlacementConfig The bucket's custom placement configuration for Custom Dual Regions.
---@field defaultEventBasedHold? boolean The default value for event-based hold on newly created objects in this bucket. Event-based hold is a way to retain objects indefinitely until an event occurs, signified by the hold's release. After being released, such objects will be subject to bucket-level retention (if any). One sample use case of this flag is for banks to hold loan documents for at least 3 years after loan is paid in full. Here, bucket-level retention is 3 years and the event is loan being paid in full. In this example, these objects will be held intact for any number of years until the event has occurred (event-based hold on the object is released) and then 3 more years after that. That means retention duration of the objects begins from the moment event-based hold transitioned from true to false. Objects under event-based hold cannot be deleted, overwritten or archived until the hold is removed.
---@field defaultObjectAcl? azure.gcpconnector.GcpBucketPropertiesDefaultObjectAclList Default access controls to apply to new objects when no ACL is provided.
---@field encryption? azure.gcpconnector.GcpBucketPropertiesEncryption Encryption configuration for a bucket.
---@field etag? string HTTP 1.1 Entity tag for the bucket.
---@field hierarchicalNamespace? azure.gcpconnector.GcpBucketPropertiesHierarchicalNamespace The bucket's hierarchical namespace configuration.
---@field iamConfiguration? azure.gcpconnector.GcpBucketPropertiesIamConfiguration The bucket's IAM configuration.
---@field id? string The ID of the bucket. For buckets, the id and name properties are the same.
---@field generation? string The content generation of this object. Used for object versioning..
---@field kind? string The kind of item this is. For buckets, this is always storage#bucket.
---@field labels? azure.gcpconnector.GcpBucketPropertiesLabelsMap User-provided labels, in key/value pairs.
---@field lifecycle? azure.gcpconnector.GcpBucketPropertiesLifecycle The bucket's lifecycle configuration. See lifecycle management for more information.
---@field location? string The location of the bucket. Object data for objects in the bucket resides in physical storage within this region. Defaults to US. See the developer's guide for the authoritative list.
---@field locationType? string The type of the bucket location.
---@field logging? azure.gcpconnector.GcpBucketPropertiesLogging The bucket's logging configuration, which defines the destination bucket and optional name prefix for the current bucket's logs.
---@field metageneration? string The metadata generation of this bucket.
---@field name? string The name of the bucket.
---@field objectRetention? azure.gcpconnector.GcpBucketPropertiesObjectRetention The bucket's object retention config.
---@field owner? azure.gcpconnector.GcpBucketPropertiesOwner The owner of the bucket. This is always the project team's owner group.
---@field projectNumber? string The project number of the project the bucket belongs to.
---@field retentionPolicy? azure.gcpconnector.GcpBucketPropertiesRetentionPolicy The bucket's retention policy. The retention policy enforces a minimum retention time for all objects contained in the bucket, based on their creation time. Any attempt to overwrite or delete objects younger than the retention period will result in a PERMISSION_DENIED error. An unlocked retention policy can be modified or removed from the bucket via a storage.buckets.update operation. A locked retention policy cannot be removed or shortened in duration for the lifetime of the bucket. Attempting to remove or decrease period of a locked retention policy will result in a PERMISSION_DENIED error.
---@field rpo? string The Recovery Point Objective (RPO) of this bucket. Set to ASYNC_TURBO to turn on Turbo Replication on a bucket.
---@field satisfiesPZS? boolean Reserved for future use.
---@field selfLink? string The URI of this bucket.
---@field softDeletePolicy? azure.gcpconnector.GcpBucketPropertiesSoftDeletePolicy The bucket's soft delete policy, which defines the period of time that soft-deleted objects will be retained, and cannot be permanently deleted.
---@field storageClass? string The bucket's default storage class, used whenever no storageClass is specified for a newly-created object. This defines how objects in the bucket are stored and determines the SLA and the cost of storage. Values include MULTI_REGIONAL, REGIONAL, STANDARD, NEARLINE, COLDLINE, ARCHIVE, and DURABLE_REDUCED_AVAILABILITY. If this value is not specified when the bucket is created, it will default to STANDARD. For more information, see storage classes.
---@field timeCreated? string The creation time of the bucket in RFC 3339 format.
---@field updated? string The modification time of the bucket in RFC 3339 format.
---@field versioning? azure.gcpconnector.GcpBucketPropertiesVersioning The bucket's versioning configuration.
---@field website? azure.gcpconnector.GcpBucketPropertiesWebsite The bucket's website configuration, controlling how the service behaves when accessing bucket contents as a web site. See the Static Website Examples for more information.

