---NodePool contains the name and configuration for a cluster's node pool. Node pools are a set of nodes (i.e. VM's), with a common configuration and specification, under the control of the cluster master. They may have a set of Kubernetes labels applied to them, which may be used to reference them during pod scheduling. They may also be resized up or down, to accommodate the workload.
---@class azure.gcpconnector.NodePool
---@field autoscaling? azure.gcpconnector.NodePoolAutoscaling Autoscaler configuration for this NodePool. Autoscaler is enabled only if a valid configuration is present.
---@field bestEffortProvisioning? azure.gcpconnector.BestEffortProvisioning Enable best effort provisioning for nodes
---@field conditions? azure.gcpconnector.NodePoolConditionsList Which conditions caused the current node pool state.
---@field config? azure.gcpconnector.NodeConfig The node configuration of the pool.
---@field etag? string This checksum is computed by the server based on the value of node pool fields, and may be sent on update requests to ensure the client has an up-to-date value before proceeding.
---@field initialNodeCount? number The initial node count for the pool. You must ensure that your Compute Engine [resource quota](https://cloud.google.com/compute/quotas) is sufficient for this number of instances. You must also have available firewall and routes quota.
---@field instanceGroupUrls? azure.gcpconnector.NodePoolInstanceGroupUrlsList [Output only] The resource URLs of the [managed instance groups](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/instance-groups/creating-groups-of-managed-instances) associated with this node pool. During the node pool blue-green upgrade operation, the URLs contain both blue and green resources.
---@field locations? azure.gcpconnector.NodePoolLocationsList The list of Google Compute Engine [zones](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/zones#available) in which the NodePool's nodes should be located. If this value is unspecified during node pool creation, the [Cluster.Locations](https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/reference/rest/v1/projects.locations.clusters#Cluster.FIELDS.locations) value will be used, instead. Warning: changing node pool locations will result in nodes being added and/or removed.
---@field management? azure.gcpconnector.NodeManagement NodeManagement configuration for this NodePool.
---@field maxPodsConstraint? azure.gcpconnector.MaxPodsConstraint The constraint on the maximum number of pods that can be run simultaneously on a node in the node pool.
---@field name? string The name of the node pool.
---@field networkConfig? azure.gcpconnector.NodeNetworkConfig Networking configuration for this NodePool. If specified, it overrides the cluster-level defaults.
---@field placementPolicy? azure.gcpconnector.PlacementPolicy Specifies the node placement policy.
---@field podIpv4CidrSize? number [Output only] The pod CIDR block size per node in this node pool.
---@field queuedProvisioning? azure.gcpconnector.QueuedProvisioning Specifies the configuration of queued provisioning.
---@field selfLink? string [Output only] Server-defined URL for the resource.
---@field status? azure.gcpconnector.NodePoolStatus|string [Output only] The status of the nodes in this pool instance.
---@field statusMessage? string [Output only] Deprecated. Use conditions instead. Additional information about the current status of this node pool instance, if available.
---@field updateInfo? azure.gcpconnector.UpdateInfo Output only. [Output only] Update info contains relevant information during a node pool update.
---@field upgradeSettings? azure.gcpconnector.UpgradeSettings Upgrade settings control disruption and speed of the upgrade.
---@field version? string The version of Kubernetes running on this NodePool's nodes. If unspecified, it defaults as described [here](https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/versioning#specifying_node_version).

---Node pool configs that apply to all auto-provisioned node pools in autopilot clusters and node auto-provisioning enabled clusters
